From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:19:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: send a TDM slot mapping only for a set
 channel map

q6afe_tdm_port_prepare() always allocates and sends a slot mapping
(AFE_PARAM_ID_PORT_SLOT_MAPPING_CONFIG), filled from the channel map, even
when the machine driver never called set_channel_map(). The MSM8996 ADSP
then rejects port start with ADSP_EBADPARAM: it does not accept a slot
mapping for a TDM port alone in its group, not even a valid one, and the
downstream driver never sends one with a single group.

Only send the slot mapping once a channel map was set. Without it this
firmware places channel n at byte offset 4 * n of the frame.

Also free a mapping left from an earlier prepare instead of leaking it.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096), primary and quaternary TDM.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c |  2 ++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c     | 14 ++++++++++++++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.h     |  1 +
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
index 93c46c6a61..26bf8f6af6 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -234,6 +234,7 @@ static int q6tdm_set_channel_map(struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
 				tdm->ch_mapping[i] = Q6AFE_CMAP_INVALID;
 
 			tdm->num_channels = tx_num;
+			tdm->ch_mapping_valid = true;
 		} else {
 			/* rx */
 			if (!rx_slot) {
@@ -253,6 +254,7 @@ static int q6tdm_set_channel_map(struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
 				tdm->ch_mapping[i] = Q6AFE_CMAP_INVALID;
 
 			tdm->num_channels = rx_num;
+			tdm->ch_mapping_valid = true;
 		}
 
 		break;
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 5e796e9206..07bc9d49a0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -1410,6 +1410,20 @@ void q6afe_tdm_port_prepare(struct q6afe_port *port,
 
 	pcfg->tdm_cfg.slot_width = cfg->slot_width;
 	pcfg->tdm_cfg.slot_mask = cfg->slot_mask;
+
+	kfree(port->scfg);
+	port->scfg = NULL;
+
+	/*
+	 * Older ADSP firmware (MSM8996) rejects a slot mapping for a TDM port
+	 * that is alone in its group (the downstream driver never sends one
+	 * with a single group) and then puts channel n at byte offset 4 * n
+	 * of the frame. Only send one when the machine driver set a channel
+	 * map.
+	 */
+	if (!cfg->ch_mapping_valid)
+		return;
+
 	port->scfg = kzalloc_obj(*port->scfg);
 	if (!port->scfg)
 		return;
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.h b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.h
index 7bb28aaaa1..aebbd4bc99 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.h
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.h
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ struct q6afe_tdm_cfg {
 	u16	slot_mask;
 	u32	data_align_type;
 	u16	ch_mapping[AFE_MAX_CHAN_COUNT];
+	bool	ch_mapping_valid;
 };
 
 struct q6afe_cdc_dma_cfg {
